  <h1>Terms & conditions</h1>
  <p style="color:var(--muted);font-weight:700">This is a courtesy translation. In case of doubt, the <a href="/regulamin?lang=pl">Polish version</a> prevails.</p>

  <h2>§1 General</h2>
  <p>The online shop panfrikandel.pl is operated by <strong>Creditline B.V.</strong> (trading as Pan Frikandel), Torenlaan 5A/5B, Bussum, the Netherlands, Chamber of Commerce (KvK) no. 59683198, VAT: NL853603108B01. Contact: hallo@panfrikandel.pl.</p>

  <h2>§2 Products</h2>
  <p>The shop sells frozen food products. Products are delivered deep-frozen and must be placed in a freezer (-18°C) immediately upon receipt. Best-before dates are printed on the packaging.</p>

  <h2>§3 Orders and payment</h2>
  <p>Orders are placed through the website. Payments are processed by Stripe (BLIK, Przelewy24, payment cards). The sales contract is concluded when the payment is confirmed.</p>

  <h2>§4 Delivery</h2>
  <p>Delivery is made by courier within Poland in insulated packaging with dry ice, usually within 24–48 working hours of dispatch. The delivery cost is shown at checkout; above the threshold shown in the shop, delivery is free.</p>
  <p>In Płock and the surrounding area (eligibility is determined by the postcode checked in the shop) the Seller may offer delivery using its own transport. The delivery time is then agreed by phone or e-mail, usually the next working day; the cost of such delivery and the free-delivery threshold are shown at checkout.</p>

  <h2>§5 Right of withdrawal</h2>
  <p>Pursuant to Article 38(4) of the Polish Consumer Rights Act, the right of withdrawal does not apply to goods liable to deteriorate rapidly (frozen products). This does not affect your statutory rights regarding defective goods or goods not in conformity with the contract.</p>

  <h2>§6 Complaints</h2>
  <p>If your parcel arrives damaged or thawed, please contact us within 24 h of receipt, with photos, at hallo@panfrikandel.pl. We handle complaints within 14 days.</p>

  <h2>§7 Final provisions</h2>
  <p>Matters not covered here are governed by Polish law, in particular the Civil Code and the Consumer Rights Act.</p>

